{
  "_comment": "Data-driven foundation hook reconciler declaration. Flat array of {event, matcher, command, timeout?} tuples for EVERY foundation-required hook registration. install.sh Step 12.5 (the generic reconciler loop) iterates this file after the Step 12 settings.json merge and, per tuple, detect-absence-by-command-substring and append into the matching .matcher bucket (creating the bucket only when none matches), so a foundation hook that lost the array-win merge (template * user) is re-landed. Adds-only / per-COMMAND idempotent; never removes or reorders the adopter's own hooks; runs AFTER the G7-gated atomic mv so its additive mutations cannot trip G7. Tuples are enumerated VERBATIM from templates/settings.json (event/matcher/command/timeout); a future foundation hook is a one-line entry here, NOT a new Step 12.N. matcher is null for event buckets with no matcher key (UserPromptSubmit/SessionStart/Stop/SessionEnd/InstructionsLoaded). This file is in foundation-manifest.json::files[] (a FOUNDATION-REPLACE managed artifact). post-tool-use-manifest.sh (the verify-after-write hook) is added to the PostToolUse Edit|Write bucket — it shipped + manifested but was wired into NO settings/fragment/required-roster (a true orphan firing zero production sessions); the PostToolUse manifest-verify entry is its sanctioned home. The statusLine.command is a FIRST-CLASS entry here (event:'statusLine', matcher:null). Step 12.5 special-cases event=='statusLine' to re-land .statusLine.command when ABSENT or DIVERGENT from the foundation command (the shadow-merge drop the .hooks tuple loop cannot recover — settings-required-hooks declared ZERO statusLine entries earlier, so a user who shadowed statusLine left worker-statusline.sh unrecoverable).",
